#Demo file

This requires a pcap file captured using TCPdump or wireshark. So you would use those programs to create a file of type .pcap. (I am not sure it would work with the wireshark specific pcap variant -- wireshark has a "save as PCAP" argument). 

It can then be run from the command line with something like 

./speed.py 91.189.91.124 ~/ubuntu.pcap 
./speed.py 5.28.62.245 ~/wget.pcap 

The first argument is an IP address that you want traffic to/from the second argument is pre-existing pcap file.
